@bank all
// Patch 0.99.5, the user's note 14: the first rounds as a tour of checks (JB2's build, CHECKS_ON). Words by SW4 from
// JB2's stand-ins (CHECK_ROWS, ROUND_READ, RG_TOUR and the round.tour.* texts in the game). TEXTS; tips 200
// characters at most. {machine} and {thing}: the stop's name ("the fire point by the lift", or a machine's).
// A reading is what you see at a check point, plainly: no judging, no numbers of decks or days.

// ---- the job and its stops
== round.title.tour
- Your first rounds: a tour of checks
== round.tour.ask
- All as it should be?
== round.tour.checked
- Checked
== round.tour.goal
- Check {thing}
== round.tour.done
- Tour done. Anything that wasn't right is on the board, noted by you.
== round.tour.noted
- Noted on the board: {machine} isn't quite right. Someone will see to it.

// ---- a machine with no sign lines of its own, read plainly (healthy, worn, faulty)
== round.read.healthy
- Its gauge sits in the green. It runs smooth and quiet.
== round.read.worn
- Its gauge has crept towards the amber, and there's a roughness in the running.
== round.read.faulty
- Its gauge is in the red. It's labouring, and you can hear it.

// ---- the tour's green tips (15b's RG_TOUR, one per step)
== tip.tour.take
- Your first rounds are on the job board: five quick checks. Take the job, then follow the arrow.
== tip.tour.go
- Head for {machine}. The arrow knows the way.
== tip.tour.look
- You're at {machine}. Have a good look, and read what you see.
== tip.tour.mark
- Everything as it should be? Tick it off.
== tip.tour.next
- On to the next check. Follow the arrow.
== tip.tour.done
- That's the tour. Hand it in at the job board.

// ---- the check points' readings (CHECK_ROWS, round.check.<id>)
== round.check.c4-ext
- Extinguisher gauge: needle in the green. Pin and seal in place, tag dated this month.
== round.check.c4-locker
- Seal unbroken. Through the little window: masks, torches and blankets, all present.
== round.check.c4-notice
- The deck plan and the muster card are current, and easy to read from a few steps back.
== round.check.c4-panel
- You press each wall panel in turn. Every one sits flush. No rattles, no gaps.
== round.check.c4-valve
- Handle at OPEN, and the tag agrees. It turns a quarter and back without a fuss.
== round.check.c4-vent
- A steady breath of cool air through the grille. Nothing caught in it.
== round.check.c4-floor
- The non-slip strips lie flat from one end of the corridor to the other. No curled corners.
== round.check.c4-smoke
- The little green light blinks every few seconds, just as it should.
== round.check.c4-exit
- The sign glows evenly. You press the test button, and it flashes bright.
== round.check.c4-door
- It slides open and shut smoothly, and stops dead when you put a hand in the way.
== round.check.c5-ext
- Needle in the green, pin in, seal whole. The tag is this month's.
== round.check.c5-notice
- The muster point is marked plainly, and the card has this month's date on it.
== round.check.c5-hatch
- The hatch seal is soft and whole all the way round, and the wheel turns easily.
== round.check.c5-vent
- Cool air through the grille. Every louvre's open.
== round.check.c5-latch
- Every latch clicks home first time. The hold's tidy.
== round.check.c5-strap
- Straps tight, buckles locked, and not a frayed edge on any of them.
== round.check.c5-lane
- The amber floor lights along the cart lane are lit, end to end.
== round.check.c5-water
- Hot and cold both run clear. The filter light shows green.
== round.check.c5-clock
- It shows the right ship time, and takes a card first go.
== round.check.c3-ext
- Gauge in the green, pin and seal in place. Somebody's polished the cylinder.
== round.check.c3-call
- Both buttons light when you press them, and the car is on its way.
== round.check.c3-vent
- Air moving steadily, and the grille's clean enough to see through.
== round.check.c3-rail
- Firm all the way along. You give each bracket a tug. None of them moves.
== round.check.c3-path
- Every path light along the promenade is on and steady.
== round.check.c3-smoke
- Green light, blinking steady as a heartbeat.
== round.check.c3-drain
- You tip a jug of water down it. Gone in a second, and the grate's clean.
== round.check.c3-cold
- The seal grips all the way round. The door thermometer reads three degrees.
== round.check.c3-fountain
- A good steady stream, and properly cold.
== round.check.c3-hose
- Every joint is dry, and every clip is tight.
== round.check.c3-lamp
- All the lights on and even. No flicker anywhere.
== round.check.c3-aid
- Sealed, full, and everything in it in date.
